A Customer Churn Prediction system predicts whether a customer is likely to leave a company/service.
Example:
A telecom company wants to know which customers may stop using their service.
The model analyzes customer details like:
monthly charges
contract type
internet service
payment method
tenure
Then predicts:
Yes → Customer may leave
No → Customer will stay
This helps companies:
reduce customer loss
improve business strategies
target risky customers with offers

Algorithms Used
1. Random Forest
Uses many decision trees
Good accuracy
Easy to understand
Shows feature importance
2. XGBoost
Advanced boosting algorithm
Very high performance
Common in competitions


Extra Things You Can Add Later
To make project stronger:
Hyperparameter tuning
ROC-AUC curve
